<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-S&amp;P upgrades two Victorian securitised issues.</title>
<headline>RTRS-S&amp;P upgrades two Victorian securitised issues.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ratings Agency Standard and Poor's Corp said on Thursday it had raised the ratings of two issues of mortgage backed securities to AA-plus from AA as a result of the upgrade of the Australian state of Victoria.  </p>
<p>The upgraded securities were issued by Victorian Housing Bonds Ltd, and comprise A$475.8 million of inflation indexed bonds and A$109.0 million of capital indexed bonds.</p>
<p>S&amp;P said the upgrades followed its earlier announcement that Victoria was being upgraded to AA-plus from AA.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
